Z||000005||Ferrari355||05-04-2000||05:42 PM||||Hey, thanks for the info on your website. It was pretty good. About the wiring harness, does it just snapoff somewhere or is it a big deal to get too. And i was wondering, the sailpanels on the fastback don't need to come off right? Oh, on the ground effects, there are these rivets. do i just break them off or is there a special way to get them off. And on the fast/notch swap, is there any major work needed to be done to do the swap like welding or does it just unsnap and bolt up? Let me know, if any of you would like to call me and ask about it to make it easier my phone number is (405)-374-9029 ask for alex and call after 3 pm central time and if they ask who it is say your name and that your from the fiero fourm. Well i better go, TTYL bye...<BR>                -Alex...||||reg||12
Z||000006||Phil||05-04-2000||06:40 PM||||There are no aterations that have to be made to the donee, just unbolt from the donor and bolt on to the other.  Fieros are the same under the skin||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||05-04-2000||06:40 PM||||There are no aterations that have to be made to the donee, just unbolt from the donor and bolt on to the other.  Fieros are the same under the skin||||reg||1
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||05-04-2000||08:00 PM||||Phil is right... the chassis are the same. The wiring harness runs from the junction box near the battery then down the passengers side then around the rear for the tail lights then around the drivers side, under the clip to the cruise control. After the clip is off the harness is easily reached.<P>The GT sail windows can stay in, but the notchback sail panels need to come out because there is a bolt behind them that has to be removed. The molding that runs between the doors and rear wheels is kinda tricky. I got mine off by pulling on them, but the fasteners broke, but new ones were like 5 dollars including the rivets that attatch the molding inside the door.<P>As far as the groundfx... I'm not too sure about them, but I think the rivets have to be drilled out and replaced with new ones. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Rodrv6||05-05-2000||09:08 PM||||There is a possible difficulty with the wire harness. On the 84's the plug where the tail light harness plugs into the main car harness is located on the firewall below the rear window almost in the center of the car. This is a rather large plug that also carries part of the engine wire harness.  Beginning in 85 the plug was moved to the right side by the battery so that the V-6 engine would fit.  I'm afraid the tail light harness from the GT is going to be a couple of feet short of reaching the plug on the 84. Also, the tail light harness on the 84 runs around the left side of the car to the back end.  85's and newer run around the right side to the back.  It's not an impossible job, but it also won't be a simple plug in job either.||||reg||4
Z||000010||Cooter||05-05-2000||09:28 PM||||The tail light wiring harness from a fastback and a coupe are different and they are not interchangeable!!!!! SCCA probably wired his different than I did mine, but if you plug the tail light harness from a v6 GT into a car harness that is not a v6 GT, you will have some really weird stuff happen.||||reg||1
